id: pm-rqaqfp
title: Optional undefined result fields silently drop telemetry completion events
description: "Observed live files, docs, context and test starts without matching completion events. summarizeResult calls JSON.stringify on an optional undefined value and then reads length; the resulting TypeError is swallowed by finishTelemetryCommand before enqueue and OTLP export. Preserve bounded redacted previews while omitting JSON-absent values so successful operations retain their outcome evidence."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-10T19:23:32.361Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T19:35:21.239Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T19:35:20.472Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T19:35:20.472Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Undefined optional result fields cannot discard command_finish or OTLP spans; explicit null and redacted sensitive fields retain their meaning; real filesystem and HTTP regression fails before the fix; live command actions regain paired telemetry events.
goal: project management = context management
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: low
confidence: 100
resolution: Skip JSON-absent undefined preview values before measuring their size so completion events and OTLP spans are persisted; preserve null and sensitive-key redaction.
expected_result: Successful commands with optional undefined fields record matching completion events and OTLP spans at redacted and max capture levels without changing command results.
actual_result: The failing real HTTP negative control now passes both capture levels with matching start/finish events and empty event/span queues; fresh live context/docs/files/stats actions are paired; all 8699 tests and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage pass.
